# Forge has no LootTable.Builder in its LootTableLoadEvent (it exposes a built LootTable), so the
# Forge loot-modify path reads the loaded pools to report them as `existingPools()`.
# 1.20.1: `LootTable.pools` is a `LootPool[]` and `LootPool.entries` a `LootPoolEntry[]` (both private in the
# real jar; the decompiled tree shows them public because Fabric API's loot AW was applied to it).
accessible    field    net/minecraft/loot/LootTable    pools    [Lnet/minecraft/loot/LootPool;
# Forge 47 patches `LootTable.pools` into a `List<LootPool>`; Loom matches AW lines by descriptor when it
# widens the dev jar, so both shapes are listed (the unmatched one is skipped; the production AT drops descriptors).
accessible    field    net/minecraft/loot/LootTable    pools    Ljava/util/List;
# LootHelper.inspect reads pool entries (Fabric API widens this on Fabric; Forge needs our own AT)
accessible    field    net/minecraft/loot/LootPool    entries    [Lnet/minecraft/loot/entry/LootPoolEntry;
